=== 2026-08-20  permanent fix for BLOCKED (b): package-member reference load ===
who/where : Claude Code, local (darwin, docker linux/amd64), dc worktree
            claude/sad-allen-051dfb @ 6b236c5
why       : the 2026-08-19 workaround was out-of-tree, so feature_parity /
            regime_parity / btc_cross_parity stayed dead in the repo — every
            run since dc 3fe8e57 (2026-08-06) died on
            "attempted relative import with no known parent package" at
            mjolnir/core/features.py:11.

1. change (4 files, tests/ only; no C++, no reference source touched):
   tests/bar_parity.py  + _package_qualname()  + load_reference_pkg()
     - walks UP the __init__.py chain from the target file: the first parent
       WITHOUT __init__.py is the sys.path src root, the rest form the dotted
       name (.../mjolnir_pkg/src + mjolnir.core.features).
     - load_reference() kept AS IS and documented as the standalone loader.
       knull/ is a package too, so an "always import as a package member"
       change would have altered the load path of the one currently-green
       harness; bar_parity was left on the path that passes.
   tests/{feature,regime,btc_cross}_parity.py: --ref-feat now goes through
     load_reference_pkg. No CLI change — the src root is discovered, not
     passed — so README invocations are unchanged. regime_parity keeps
     --pkg-src: it still locates obfuscation/map.json through it.

2. no silent fallbacks (CLAUDE.md). Three explicit fail-fasts, all exercised:
     file not inside a package  -> "BLOCKED: ... is not inside a package"
     ImportError on the import  -> "BLOCKED: cannot import mjolnir.core.features",
       naming pyarrow, since the package path runs mjolnir/core/__init__.py ->
       research -> pyarrow, which the old standalone load never needed
     shadowed by another copy    -> "BLOCKED: ... resolved to /shadow/...",
       so a stray installed mjolnir cannot be graded in place of the checkout

